{%- comment -%}
  Badges on a product card: short labels like "Sin gluten" or "Nuevo", from the product's
  custom.badges metafield -- a list of `badge` metaobjects, each carrying a `label` and a `kind`.

  WHY A METAFIELD AND NOT TAGS: mionasbakery publishes two locales, es (primary) and ca, and Shopify
  tags are not translatable content. A badge stored as a tag would render its Spanish string on the
  Catalan storefront forever. A metaobject's label field is translatable. Full reasoning in
  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-03-product-card-badges-design.md.

  METAOBJECT FIELDS NEED `.value`. `badge.label.value`, not `badge.label` -- each field is a
  metafield drop. Getting this wrong renders blank labels rather than raising, so it fails silently.

  ONE BLOCK, TWO PLACEMENTS. The card mounts this twice: once as an overlay of the commercial
  badges over the image, once inline under the title for the dietary ones. `kind` is what routes
  them, which is why it is a constrained choice on the metaobject rather than a free string.

  ITS OWN COMPONENT, INHERITING FROM NOTHING. The theme and ../design-system both contain
  badge-adjacent things -- ProductPromoCard's promo flag, Stamp's eyebrow, Horizon's sale/sold-out
  chip. None of them is the precedent here, by the store owner's explicit decision. Recorded so
  nobody reunifies them later: the promo flag is a marketing device on a different card, this is a
  per-product property, and they are allowed to diverge.

  So: no --product-promo-card-badge-* here, no reuse of blocks/mionas-stamp.liquid's .mionas-stamp
  class, no --stamp-base-* tokens.

  ITS TOKENS LIVE BELOW, NOT IN assets/design-tokens.css. That file is auto-generated by
  scripts/sync-design-tokens.mjs from ../design-system and says "Do not edit directly" on line 1 --
  anything added there is wiped by the next `npm run tokens:sync`. A theme-only component declares
  its custom properties on its own root class, which survives a sync and keeps them next to the
  rules that spend them. Their values are token PRIMITIVES (--space-*, --radius-*, --brand-*,
  --color-*), never another component's tokens: spending primitives keeps the theme coherent,
  spending a neighbour's component tokens couples the two.

  THE OVERLAY NEEDS NO NATIVE EDIT AND NO FORK. Horizon emits its own sale/sold-out badge from
  inside blocks/_product-card-gallery.liquid because .product-badges is absolute against
  .card-gallery (snippets/card-gallery.liquid:240), and that block accepts no children. But
  .product-card__content is ALSO already position: relative (assets/base.css:116), so an overlay
  child of the card pins to the card box with no new positioning rule anywhere.

  KNOWN COLLISION: Horizon's native Sale/Sold out badge sits at the corner set in theme settings
  (settings.badge_position). If that corner matches this block's Corner setting, the two overlap.
  Not detected here -- the theme setting is global and this block is per-placement, so any
  automatic move would be a guess about which one should yield. It is a merchandising fix: put the
  native badges on the opposite corner.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
  assign block_settings = block.settings
  assign badges = product.metafields.custom.badges.value

  assign kind_filter = block_settings.kind | default: 'all'
  assign placement = block_settings.placement | default: 'inline'
  assign size = block_settings.size | default: 'label-sm'

  # snippets/mionas-text.liquid takes variant/size as two params now; `size` above is still the
  # fixed-band "label-<size>" value this block's own Size setting stores, so split off the step
  # once here rather than per badge in the loop below (`render` args can't take an inline filter).
  assign size_step = size | split: '-' | last
-%}

{%- if badges != blank -%}
  {%- capture items -%}
    {%- for badge in badges -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign badge_kind = badge.kind.value
        assign badge_label = badge.label.value

        comment
          snippets/mionas-text.liquid outputs `content` unfiltered and says so in its doc: callers
          sanitise. This is merchant-authored text out of a metaobject, so it is escaped here.
        endcomment
        assign badge_label = badge_label | escape

        comment
          Both kinds render at the role's `default` variant. The commercial fill's foreground is
          this component's own token, applied by the two-classes-deep rule in the stylesheet, so it
          does not borrow a role variant to get its colour.
        endcomment
        assign badge_variant = 'default'

        assign badge_class = 'mionas-product-badges__badge mionas-product-badges__badge--' | append: badge_kind
      -%}
      {%- if badge_label != blank -%}
        {%- if kind_filter == 'all' or kind_filter == badge_kind -%}
          <li class="mionas-product-badges__item">
            {%- render 'mionas-text',
              content: badge_label,
              variant: 'label',
              size: size_step,
              color: badge_variant,
              tag: 'span',
              class: badge_class
            -%}
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The gate is on the captured items, not on `badges`: a product can carry badges of which none
    match this instance's Kind filter, and an empty <ul> would still take its gap slot in the card's
    flex column. Same reflex as blocks/mionas-text.liquid's visible_text check.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign has_items = items | strip -%}

  {%- if has_items != blank -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign list_class = 'mionas-product-badges spacing-style mionas-product-badges--' | append: placement
      if placement == 'overlay'
        assign corner = block_settings.corner | default: 'top-left'
        assign list_class = list_class | append: ' mionas-product-badges--' | append: corner
      endif
    -%}
    {%- capture list_style -%}
      {%- render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    <ul
      class="{{ list_class }}"
      style="{{ list_style }}"
      {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
    >
      {{- items -}}
    </ul>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* This component's tokens. They live here rather than in assets/design-tokens.css, which is
     auto-generated from ../design-system and would drop them on the next `npm run tokens:sync`.
     Every value is a primitive, never another component's token -- see the header comment. */
  .mionas-product-badges {
    --mionas-product-badge-radius: var(--radius-full);
    --mionas-product-badge-padding-block: var(--space-3xs);
    --mionas-product-badge-padding-inline: var(--space-xs);
    --mionas-product-badge-gap: var(--space-2xs);
    --mionas-product-badge-letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    --mionas-product-badge-commercial-background: var(--brand-accent);
    --mionas-product-badge-commercial-foreground: var(--brand-accent-inverse);
    --mionas-product-badge-dietary-border-color: var(--color-warm-300);

    display: flex;
    gap: var(--mionas-product-badge-gap);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* Several badges is the normal case, so each placement lays its list out for it: the inline row
     wraps onto a second line rather than truncating, and the overlay stacks down the corner rather
     than running sideways across the photo. */
  .mionas-product-badges--inline {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .mionas-product-badges--overlay {
    /* Absolute against .product-card__content, which base.css:116 already makes position: relative.
       The inset clears the card's own corner radius, the same trick --badge-inset uses in
       snippets/product-badges-styles.liquid:10 -- a badge sitting at a flat 8px from a 16px-radius
       corner visually collides with the curve. */
    --mionas-product-badges-inset: max(var(--space-xs), calc(var(--card-base-radius) * (1 - cos(45deg))));

    position: absolute;
    z-index: var(--layer-flat);
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;

    /* The whole card is a link (snippets/product-card.liquid:80) and these badges are not
       interactive, so they must never intercept the click. */
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .mionas-product-badges--top-left {
    top: var(--mionas-product-badges-inset);
    left: var(--mionas-product-badges-inset);
  }

  .mionas-product-badges--top-right {
    top: var(--mionas-product-badges-inset);
    right: var(--mionas-product-badges-inset);
  }

  .mionas-product-badges--bottom-left {
    bottom: var(--mionas-product-badges-inset);
    left: var(--mionas-product-badges-inset);
  }

  /* TWO CLASSES DEEP ON PURPOSE, exactly as blocks/mionas-stamp.liquid documents: every
     .text-role--<role> sets font-weight and letter-spacing from a single-class selector in this
     same compiled bundle, so equal specificity would leave the winner to source order.
     No font-size, line-height or color here -- those come from the role and the variant. */
  .text-role.mionas-product-badges__badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--mionas-product-badge-padding-block) var(--mionas-product-badge-padding-inline);
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: var(--mionas-product-badge-radius);
    letter-spacing: var(--mionas-product-badge-letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* Loud, because it is promotion. */
  .text-role.mionas-product-badges__badge--commercial {
    background: var(--mionas-product-badge-commercial-background);
    color: var(--mionas-product-badge-commercial-foreground);
  }

  /* Quiet, because it is a fact. Same shape and size as the commercial one so the two read as one
     family; only the fill differs. The transparent border above is what keeps them the same size. */
  .text-role.mionas-product-badges__badge--dietary {
    border-color: var(--mionas-product-badge-dietary-border-color);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Product badges",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "kind",
      "label": "Kind",
      "options": [
        { "value": "all", "label": "All" },
        { "value": "dietary", "label": "Dietary" },
        { "value": "commercial", "label": "Commercial" }
      ],
      "default": "dietary",
      "info": "Which badges from the product's Badges metafield this instance renders."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "placement",
      "label": "Placement",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inline", "label": "Inline" },
        { "value": "overlay", "label": "Overlay" }
      ],
      "default": "inline",
      "info": "Overlay pins the badges to a corner of the card, over the image."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "corner",
      "label": "Corner",
      "options": [
        { "value": "top-left", "label": "Top left" },
        { "value": "top-right", "label": "Top right" },
        { "value": "bottom-left", "label": "Bottom left" }
      ],
      "default": "top-left",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.placement == 'overlay' }}",
      "info": "Avoid the corner used by the theme's own Sale and Sold out badges, or they overlap."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "size",
      "label": "Size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "label-lg", "label": "Large" },
        { "value": "label-md", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "label-sm", "label": "Small" }
      ],
      "default": "label-sm",
      "info": "The label-band size the badges render at, the same ladder as Mionas: Text."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-start",
      "label": "t:settings.left",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-end",
      "label": "t:settings.right",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Product badges",
      "category": "t:categories.product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
